/AP << /N 866 0 R >> /Contents (This paper focused on the unordered rectangular pieces which are of different sizes, e.g the brick wall of the same width, including missing pieces\012the method was based on the dissimilarity between two fragments, calculate the Euclidean distance of edge info.\012some problems:\0121. the best one might be incorrect.\0122. the slot of the suitable neighbour could be occupied by other piece \012the further research: \0121.how to predict the correctness of the offset\0122.could the number of the pixels impact the accuracy )
/T (yanxia) >> /AAPL:AKAnnotationObject ()
>> /F 4 /BS << /W 0 >> /Subtype /FreeText /DA (//Helvetica 12 Tf 0 g) /Border
[ 0 0 0 ] /Type /Annot /Rect [ 114.4051 684.0575 553.1767 752.3064 ] /M (D:20260417185132Z00'00')
/AP << /N 873 0 R >> /Contents (This paper focused on the unordered rectangular pieces which are of different sizes, e.g the brick wall of the same width, including missing pieces\012the method was based on the dissimilarity between two fragments, calculate the Euclidean distance of edge info.\012some problems:\0121. the best one might be incorrect.\0122. the slot of the suitable neighbour could be occupied by other piece \012the further research: \0121.how to predict the correctness of the offset\0122.could the number of the pixels impact the accuracy )
/T (yanxia) >>
endobj
